{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"scripts/bin/harness-cli --help && rg -n \\\"intake (add|record)|harness-cli intake|intake\\\" docs scripts -g '*.md' -g '*.sh' -g '*.py' | head -120\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"scripts/bin/harness-cli --help && rg -n \\\"intake (add|record)|harness-cli intake|intake\\\" docs scripts -g '*.md' -g '*.sh' -g '*.py' | head -120\"","aggregated_output":"durable layer for the project harness\n\nUsage: harness-cli <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  init           Create the harness database if it does not already exist\n  migrate        Apply schema migrations\n  import         Seed or refresh the database from existing markdown state\n  intake         Record a feature intake classification\n  story          Add or update a story\n  decision       Add a decision or run its verification\n  backlog        Add or close a backlog item\n  tool           Register or remove external tools\n  intervention   Record a human, review, CI, or agent intervention\n  trace          Record an agent execution trace\n  score-trace    Score a trace against the trace quality tiers\n  score-context  Score trace context reads against CONTEXT_RULES.md\n  audit          Run drift audit and entropy score\n  propose        Generate improvement proposals from observed patterns\n  db             Manage harness database changesets\n  query          Query harness data\n  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help     Print help\n  -V, --version  Print version\nscripts/agent-harness-block.md:9:  intake, or record a trace.\ndocs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md:71:`checked_at`). Run it at intake start so status reflects current reality.\ndocs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md:153:| `intake` | Task specification | Record a feature intake classification. | `--type`, `--summary`, `--lane` |\ndocs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md:190:| `query intakes` | Task specification | Show recent intake records. | none |\ndocs/HARNESS_MATURITY.md:21:- No feature intake policy exists.\ndocs/HARNESS_MATURITY.md:70:- Lane accuracy improves when agents read the intake policy.\ndocs/HARNESS_MATURITY.md:92:- `scripts/bin/harness-cli` can record intake, story, decision, backlog, and trace\ndocs/HARNESS_MATURITY.md:94:- `scripts/schema/001-init.sql` defines durable tables for intake, story,\ndocs/HARNESS_MATURITY.md:164:  quality against tier rules, `query friction` includes linked intake context,\nscripts/README.md:13:present, and do not bootstrap, initialize/migrate, record intake, or trace.\nscripts/README.md:37:scripts/bin/harness-cli intake ...    # Record a feature intake classification\nscripts/README.md:114:scripts/bin/harness-cli intake ...\nscripts/README.md:128:scripts/bin/harness-cli query intakes\ndocs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md:3:This intake gate applies to change, build, and fix requests before code or\ndocs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md:8:They do not bootstrap or initialize Harness, record intake, update a story or\ndocs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md:49:Do not create or extend a monolithic spec by default after intake. Use product\ndocs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md:67:- Record the intake row before implementation; tiny work skips story packet\ndocs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md:147:At the end of intake, the agent should be able to say:\ndocs/TRACE_SPEC.md:17:| `intake_id` | INTEGER | Standard+ when an intake was recorded | Integer id from the related `intake` row. | `36` |\ndocs/TRACE_SPEC.md:54:- `intake_id` when an intake was recorded.\ndocs/TRACE_SPEC.md:104:| Normal | Standard | Record intake, actions, files read, files changed, outcome, and friction/errors. |\ndocs/TRACE_SPEC.md:147:  --intake 51 \\\ndocs/TRACE_SPEC.md:167:  --intake 36 \\\ndocs/TRACE_SPEC.md:189:- It does not connect to intake or stories.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:17:| Feature intake   |\ndocs/HARNESS.md:63:- Feature intake and risk lanes.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:90:Operational data — intake classifications, story status, decision outcomes,\ndocs/HARNESS.md:111:scripts/bin/harness-cli intake  --type <type> --summary <text> --lane <lane>\ndocs/HARNESS.md:226:Backlog risk uses the same lane vocabulary as intake and stories:\ndocs/HARNESS.md:241:3. Do not run bootstrap, initialize or migrate a database, record intake,\ndocs/HARNESS.md:247:or create an intake row merely to explain the failure.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:256:   classification with `scripts/bin/harness-cli intake`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:311:require a stable linked Harness-improvement intake and a completed matching\ndocs/HARNESS_COMPONENTS.md:24:| 1 | Task specification | Covered | `AGENTS.md`, `docs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md`, `docs/templates/story.md`, `docs/templates/spec-intake.md`, `docs/templates/high-risk-story/*`, `docs/stories/*`, `intake` table, `story` table | Requests are classified by type and lane before implementation; normal and high-risk work have templates and durable story rows. | Keep story packets synchronized with future product docs. |\ndocs/HARNESS_COMPONENTS.md:28:| 5 | Task state | Covered | `scripts/bin/harness-cli query matrix`, `docs/TEST_MATRIX.md`, `intake` table, `story` table, `trace` table | Durable records track intake, story status, proof columns, and task traces. | Add lifecycle checks so in-progress stories cannot be forgotten. |\ndocs/HARNESS_COMPONENTS.md:30:| 7 | Failure attribution | Partial | `docs/HARNESS_COMPONENTS.md`, `docs/TRACE_SPEC.md`, `trace.errors`, `trace.harness_friction`, `docs/HARNESS_BACKLOG.md`, `backlog` table, `scripts/bin/harness-cli query friction` | Failures can be tied to files, components, friction, backlog proposals, and linked intake lane/type context. | No automated attribution from benchmark failures to harness components exists yet. |\ndocs/HARNESS_COMPONENTS.md:43:| Middleware | installer safety logic, feature intake workflow | Partial | The installer and intake process mediate work, but there is no runtime middleware enforcing policies. |\ndocs/HARNESS_COMPONENTS.md:87:| `docs/decisions/0003-generic-spec-intake-harness.md` | Project memory | Task specification |\ndocs/HARNESS_COMPONENTS.md:121:| `docs/templates/spec-intake.md` | Task specification | Context selection |\ndocs/IMPROVEMENT_PROTOCOL.md:91:next `harness_improvement` intake command. Rejection records one terminal reason\ndocs/IMPROVEMENT_PROTOCOL.md:92:and covered evidence without creating an intake, story, or orchestrated run.\ndocs/CONTEXT_RULES.md:16:| Read-only | answer, explain, review, diagnose, plan, status | None. Do not bootstrap, initialize/migrate, record intake, update durable state, or trace. | `AGENTS.md`, the exact files or output named by the request, then the smallest adjacent source needed to support the answer. |\ndocs/CONTEXT_RULES.md:17:| Change | change, build, fix | Bootstrap first, then intake, story/proof, trace, and backlog mutations as the selected lane requires. | `AGENTS.md`, `docs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md`, focused active matrix summary, then lane- and trigger-specific sources below. |\ndocs/CONTEXT_RULES.md:21:that migration is a change request, so bootstrap and intake happen before the\ndocs/CONTEXT_RULES.md:125:| High-risk | About 10K tokens of Harness context | Full intake, architecture, relevant decisions, high-risk templates, product docs, validation docs, trace spec, and component/maturity docs when Harness behavior changes. | High-risk work needs source hierarchy, prior decisions, and proof expectations in context before implementation. |\ndocs/CONTEXT_RULES.md:138:answer is supported. For a change request, `AGENTS.md` points to intake and the\ndocs/GLOSSARY.md:86:intake, planning, implementation, validation, or trace recording.\ndocs/GLOSSARY.md:107:(intakes, stories, decisions, backlog items, traces) as structured, queryable\ndocs/stories/backlog.md:13:| TBD | Add candidate epics after spec intake | unsliced |\ndocs/README.md:27:- `templates/`: reusable spec-intake, story, plan, decision, and validation\ndocs/stories/README.md:20:Use `docs/templates/high-risk-story/` when the feature intake classifies work as\ndocs/decisions/0001-harness-first-development.md:27:- Feature intake and risk lanes.\ndocs/decisions/0003-generic-spec-intake-harness.md:18:intake, story, proof, and decision loop.\ndocs/decisions/0003-generic-spec-intake-harness.md:28:- Empty product docs except for intake guidance.\ndocs/decisions/0003-generic-spec-intake-harness.md:53:- The first spec intake must create product docs and candidate epics before\ndocs/decisions/0003-generic-spec-intake-harness.md:58:- Add a spec-intake template if repeated projects reveal a stable format.\ndocs/decisions/0005-prebuilt-rust-harness-cli.md:44:- Application: use cases for intake, stories, decisions, backlog, traces, and\ndocs/decisions/0004-sqlite-durable-layer.md:16:- There is no structured way to query past intakes, traces, or friction reports.\ndocs/decisions/0002-post-spec-product-lifecycle.md:7:Superseded by `0003-generic-spec-intake-harness.md`\ndocs/decisions/0002-post-spec-product-lifecycle.md:45:- Future work keeps using the same intake, story, proof, and harness-growth\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
