alidation.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:84:that require executable proof.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:146:  behavior-to-proof control panel backed by the durable layer\ndocs/HARNESS.md:160:validation expectations during the first buildout.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:164:stories, durable proof records, and decision records.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:175:- Harness improvement: a process, template, proof, or agent-instruction change.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:184:  -> define validation proof\ndocs/HARNESS.md:186:  -> update product docs, stories, durable proof records, and decisions\ndocs/HARNESS.md:192:product docs, candidate stories, validation shape, open decisions, and exit\ndocs/HARNESS.md:200:When an agent is confused, repeats manual reasoning, needs a new validation\ndocs/HARNESS.md:209:behavior or validation results:\ndocs/HARNESS.md:257:3. Check focused proof status with\ndocs/HARNESS.md:263:6. Before finishing, ask whether product truth, validation expectations,\ndocs/HARNESS.md:274:Stories may carry a mechanical proof command:\ndocs/HARNESS.md:293:`story add --verify` or `story update --verify`. Record proof booleans with\ndocs/HARNESS.md:297:Use `scripts/bin/harness-cli query matrix --numeric` when copying proof values\ndocs/HARNESS.md:302:evidence text while retaining lane, runnable state, and proof columns.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:306:proof view.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:309:It requires an `in_progress` or `changed` story, runs fresh proof, and marks the\ndocs/HARNESS.md:310:story implemented only when that proof passes. Resolver stories additionally\ndocs/HARNESS.md:313:proof and eligible accepted backlog closures are committed atomically and\ndocs/HARNESS.md:316:proof, evidence, and verification-command updates remain available. Ordinary\ndocs/HARNESS.md:317:`story verify` and `story verify-all` remain proof-only.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:368:validation changes, record the decision in both places:\ndocs/HARNESS.md:403:- Removing validation requirements.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:426:No validation scripts exist yet. When implementation